el system  some of these are metastatic and some  are not they segregate and it gives you  a unique opportunity to study those  pre-cancerous lesions that are the most  important versus those that are the most  innocuous  in another model system  the  stat one knockout mouse which was made  as a way to  reduce natural killer t cell function  there's a nice um  cell article  from the schreiber lab that points out  that  these stat 1 knockout mice  are susceptible to obligate  intracellular pathogens like listeria  challenge but it turned out these  mice also developed mammary tumors and  they developed a unique pattern of  mammary tumor that we  think is very analogous to age-related  er positive breast cancer  which is  the most common type of breast cancer  and also  despite an overall good prognosis in the  category still the number one  cause of breast cancer death and we  asked whether  this was because of the natural killer  t-cell defect associated with a  difference in inflammation  whereby  you might hypothesize that  women as they age have reduced  ability to be  effective at  immunosurveillance or immunosuppression  of  these  age-related er positive breast cancers  and i invite you to look at this paper  in detail very interestingly it showed  that the tumor cells express  chemoattractants for macrophages but  also express  chemo  repellents for macrophages and this  resulted in macrophages that come close  to the cancer but then are not able to  attack the cancer or prevent its spread  because of the chemo repellent effects  and those segregate into extracellular  vesicle fractions and soluble fractions  which are these dot plots that are very  small down at the bottom in panels g h  and i  but i invite you to look at the camp at  the at the paper for more details  [Music]  so a few clues about  how dcis might progressing progress come  from her too i think her2 expression  it turns out in  dcis is seen  in at least  35 percent in this case compared to  